body:
Hi there,

Each of my search results has a publish date. I want to ensure that nothing with a publish date in the future shows in my results. Is there currently a way to do this using the searchParameters? Here is my current setup:

```js
const searchParametersVideo = {
  facetFilters: [["modelName:video"], ["locale:" + getAlgoliaLocale(locale)], ["publishDate:"+'<='+moment().format()]],
  hitsPerPage: 3
};

return (
  <InstantSearch
    appId={config.search.appId}
    apiKey={config.search.apiKey}
    searchParameters={searchParametersVideo}
    searchState={{query: this.props.searchState}}
    indexName={config.search.index}>
    <VirtualSearchBox/>
    <VideoResults />
  </InstantSearch>
)
```

As you can see, I have attempted to add a publishDate filter to my `facetFilters`, which does not seem to work. Does anyone know of the correct way to do this?

Thank you,
Joshua
